	(text "wire the slave (with 20% larger current limit)\nto the electrode with 10% larger effective capacitance"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.178 22.098 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a5f0fbf0-5038-4ae2-80b4-6d1be6911a01")
	)
	(text "the amount of PA79 overshoot doesn't matter; any\nshort voltage step will make the piezo resonate with\nan amplitude of twice the DAC step size\n\n...\n\ncome back to this problem tomorrow\nresonant noise ≥ 2 * DAC resolution...\n\nmaybe we can at least low-pass filter the fine Z output\nbefore summing with the coarse output in the OPA828 stage?\nmake the compensation capacitor swappable, tuning it to match\na specific resonant frequency\n\nthis filter is the second of the dual op-amp for the Z stage,\nwhich then gets fed into the summing op-amp with -1 gain\nperhaps X and Y channels should have this, and we design a board\nfor the future where there will be 6 DAC channels?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e9ea69c4-da62-40f1-8a24-9dfb45ce99bd")
	)
